# DTF tier manifest: s3-cross-repo-same-version
#   artifact-keeper#5662 (PR #5796, 1.12.0): on S3/GCS/Azure storage the
#   hosted packages of 18 formats were written to flat, repository-blind keys
#   such as `chef/<name>/<version>/<file>`. Two repositories of the same
#   format share one object namespace on a cloud backend, so publishing a
#   version that another repository already held answered 409 CONFLICT
#   "... already owned by another repository; refusing cross-repository
#   overwrite". The fix writes new objects under `<prefix>/<repository-id>/...`
#   on cloud backends.
#   Profile-set: storage.s3 (MinIO, one shared bucket).
#
# For each covered format (cran, helm, chef, puppet, rubygems, hex) the oracle
# creates two hosted repositories, publishes the same version (same bytes)
# into both with the format's native publish request, and downloads it from
# both.
#
# Gates: (CONTROL) the first publish is 2xx and downloads byte-exact (both
# images). (#5662) the second publish into the other repository is 2xx, both
# repositories then serve the published bytes, and the first repository's
# copy still downloads byte-exact.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test; the oracle drives a dozen
# publishes and two dozen downloads back-to-back.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.13 (the second publish answers 409 for every format).
# Green: ak-backend:fix-5662-9ec740a8 (PR #5796).
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
